## Key tables (dqt metadata DB)
```sql
tenants           (id, name, created_at)
users             (id, tenant_id, email, hashed_password, role, created_at)
sources           (id, tenant_id, engine, display_name, host, port, dbname,
                   username, encrypted_password, ssl_mode, extra_config, created_at)
datasets          (id, source_id, tenant_id, schema_name, table_name,
                   row_count, last_synced_at, created_at)
columns           (id, dataset_id, name, data_type, pii, owner,
                   classification, description, tags, created_at)
checks            (id, tenant_id, dataset_id, column_id, detector_slug,
                   params, baseline_config, schedule, created_at)
check_runs        (id, check_id, started_at, finished_at, verdict,
                   score, plain_english, details)
incidents         (id, tenant_id, check_id, check_run_id, opened_at,
                   resolved_at, status, severity, score, detector_slug)
incident_comments (id, incident_id, user_id, body, created_at)
audit_log         (id, tenant_id, actor_id, action, target_type,
                   target_id, payload, created_at)
```

## TimescaleDB
`check_runs` and `metric_runs` are designed to become hypertables. In MVP they use a regular `started_at` index. Migrating to a hypertable later is a single `SELECT create_hypertable(...)` call.

## pgvector
Used for semantic embeddings on column/metric descriptions. Column `embedding VECTOR(1536)` on `columns` and `metrics`. Enables similarity search in the Cmd-K palette and agent grounding.

## Row-level security
All queries pass through `TenantScopedRepository` which injects `tenant_id` automatically. RLS policies in Postgres as defense-in-depth:
```sql
ALTER TABLE datasets ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON datasets
    USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::uuid);
```

## Credentials
Warehouse credentials encrypted at rest with `cryptography.fernet`. Key from env var `DQT_CREDS_KEY`. Never store plaintext credentials in any table.

## Connection pool
10 pool / 40 overflow per server instance. Async via asyncpg.
